      "$comment": "The leading adornment keeps the input wrapper present across the clear, which is the same convention the VfInput catalog uses. Without it the Vue adapter re-renders from the bare branch into the wrapped one, replacing the input and dropping focus to body - a documented VfInput quirk that has its own approved divergence on input/interaction-wrapper-transition, and nothing to do with the field."
